# .dockerignore  v12.28.0
#
# ALLOWLIST MODEL -- remediates TNX-C-002.
#
# The previous file was a five-line denylist:
#
#     node_modules
#     .git
#     .env
#     *.log
#     data/connections.csv
#
# data/google-service-account.json was not listed, so a complete, unredacted
# RSA service-account private key was copied into every Docker image built from
# this tree. A denylist that must enumerate every secret filename will always
# eventually miss one, which is exactly what happened.
#
# This file inverts the model: everything is excluded, then the specific paths
# the runtime image needs are re-included. A newly added secret is therefore
# excluded by default and requires a deliberate, reviewable edit to ship.
#
# When adding a new runtime path, add the narrowest possible !rule below and
# state why in a comment.

# ── Exclude everything ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*

# ── Re-include only what the runtime image needs ────────────────────────────

# Application source.
!src/
!src/**

# Dependency manifest and lockfile. Both are required for `npm ci`.
!package.json
!package-lock.json

# Standalone maintenance and codegen scripts invoked by npm scripts.
!scripts/
!scripts/**

# ── Re-exclusions inside the allowed paths ──────────────────────────────────
# Nested node_modules and test artefacts must not reach the image even though
# their parent directory is allowed.
src/**/node_modules
scripts/**/node_modules
**/*.test.js
**/*.spec.js
**/*.log

# Credential material must never reach an image, under any filename, even if a
# future !rule above would otherwise admit it. Docker evaluates rules in order,
# so these trailing lines win.
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/id_rsa*
**/service-account*.json
**/*credentials*.json
**/*secret*.json
.env
.env.*
